diff --git a/docs/keyset-pagination.md b/docs/keyset-pagination.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..a0030d73b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/keyset-pagination.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# List continuation pagination
+
+Synchronous and asynchronous list handlers return `NextPageToken` when a request
+has `Take > 0`, `Skip == 0`, no `DistinctFields` (including an empty array), an
+`IIdRow` entity, and more matching rows. Send that token as `PageToken` to fetch
+the next page. Stop when `NextPageToken` is null. A missing or null `PageToken`
+starts a new listing. Ordinary offset and distinct requests continue to work,
+but do not return continuation tokens.
+
+```json
+{ "Take": 50, "Sort": ["Name"], "ExcludeTotalCount": true }
+```
+
+For the next page, repeat the request with `"PageToken": "<NextPageToken>"`.
+Keep the sort, criteria, equality filters, quick-search text and field, and
+`IncludeDeleted` unchanged. The page size and column selection may change.
+Invalid, altered, or incompatible tokens produce `ValidationError` with code
+`InvalidPageToken`. Tokens are opaque: clients should not parse or modify them.
+
+Continuation ordering uses the requested sort, or the handler's native sort,
+with the ID ascending as a unique tiebreaker unless already included. The initial
+request retains the handler's existing ordering. Required sort and ID fields
+are selected even with `KeyOnly` or column exclusions; field read permissions
+are still enforced. A sort requiring an unreadable field disables continuation
+on the initial request and rejects a continuation request.
+
+Handlers fetch at most one extra row to detect another page. That probe is not
+processed or returned. `Take` still reports the requested page size, `Skip`
+remains zero, and `TotalCount` continues to count all matching rows rather than
+only rows after the boundary. `ExcludeTotalCount` retains its existing meaning.
+
+Tokens use authenticated encryption and preserve boundary value types and
+precision. The current token key is process-scoped: application restarts
+invalidate outstanding tokens, and multi-worker deployments need worker
+affinity for a listing. A client receiving an invalid-token error can restart
+from the first page. Continuations are not database snapshots; concurrent
+changes to a row's sort values can move it across the boundary.
